  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A wide painting of a rainbow coloured city of outlined towers beside a beach and a swirling blue sea, with green parkland behind.",
    "description": "A wide landscape painting in oil on wood, with faint panel seams. A city of simple outlined towers in every colour, pink, orange, lime, blue and purple, fills the left two thirds, with a large striped drum shaped stadium at left, an oval domed building, and a few recognisable tall spires. Rows of round trees and lollipop trees fill the streets, and a pale river or road curves through the middle. On the right a cream beach with scalloped white surf meets a sea rendered as wavy bands of blue, teal and green. Behind the city, striped fields and clouds roll to the horizon under a pale sky. The forms are flat and outlined in thin brown line, with soft colour gradients inside each block.",
    "impression": "The title explains the joke: a northern city dropped on a Florida beach, with everything made cheerful and toy sized. It has the feel of a souvenir postcard painted from memory. The stadium and the spires are the clues that it is somewhere real, while the colours insist it is not.",
